WEBVTT

00:00:12.050 --> 00:00:13.340
Hana!

00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:14.550
Can I come in?

00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:15.850
Sure.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:20.230
Your high school uniform is ready.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.100
Here, Hana.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:31.440
I know this is sudden, but try it on.

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:39.330
Wh-What do you think?

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:41.790
It's adorable!

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:46.710
R-Really? I hope it's okay.

00:00:47.290 --> 00:00:49.210
Of course it's okay.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:50.880
You look cute!

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.010
M-More importantly, Shion...

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:58.720
Um, do I really look like
a first year high school student?

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:06.100
Don't worry! Instead of a high school student,
you could pass for middle school student.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.320
N-Now I hope that's not true.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:11.230
Oh, wait!

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.000
Do I look like a first year high school student?

00:01:27.580 --> 00:01:29.460
I-I don't know about that...

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.380
Sh-Shion!

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.300
Hana, smile!

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.760
You don't have to take a photo!

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:38.760
It's embarrassing...

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:41.850
Then why don't we take a picture together?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.680
Maybe we should take it outside.

00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:47.900
I don't know if it's a good idea
for you to wear that outside!

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.570
THE FIRST BUTTERFLIES

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:24.910
"At last, it's the opening ceremony. I'm off."

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:24.910
TO MOM

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.120
Send.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.000
GOOD LUCK
MOM

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.830
Mom...

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:35.380
From Dad too...

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:37.590
Another mail from Mom?

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:38.210
YOU HAVEN'T FORGOTTEN ANYTHING, HAVE YOU?
MOM

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:38.970
YOU HAVE RECEIVED A MAIL FROM DAD

00:03:38.970 --> 00:03:40.720
YOU MAY BE GETTING MAIL FROM YOUR MOTHER TOO,
BUT I JUST WANTED TO SAY KEEP YOUR CHIN UP,
STUDY HARD, AND ENJOY THE NEW SCHOOL YEAR WITH FRIENDS!
I'M ALWAYS THINKING ABOUT YOU!
MOM IS ALWAYS THINKING ABOUT YOU TOO!
DAD

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:40.010
Again?!

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:41.590
YOU HAVE RECEIVED A MAIL FROM MOM

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:45.560
<i>Dad's mail is being drowned out.</i>

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.680
HOSHIO PRIVATE GIRLS ACADEMY
ENTRANCE CEREMONY

00:03:51.690 --> 00:03:54.020
And that ends the entrance ceremony.

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.320
I was so nervous!

00:03:59.940 --> 00:04:02.610
Am I really a high school student now?

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:08.450
Ow!

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:13.710
Um...

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.090
Kamuri?

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.300
Sorry. You look so much like a girl I know...

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:23.130
Eiko...

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:25.140
It is you?

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:26.600
Eiko...

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.980
I mean, you...
you haven't changed since then...

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:32.440
Eiko!

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.060
Kamuri!

00:04:37.650 --> 00:04:39.690
You really haven't changed,

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.650
even though I haven't seen you
since elementary school.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:48.910
Rapid growth!

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:51.200
I'm a growing child, after all.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:55.040
You sure are! You've grown a lot.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:05:00.130
I see. Everyone has friends
from elementary school or middle school.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.720
<i>They're all friends already.</i>

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.520
Good morning!

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:12.520
G-Good morning!

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:13.480
Huh?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.690
- Good morning!
- Morning!

00:05:18.020 --> 00:05:19.770
- Good morning!
- Morning.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.320
Good morning!

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:23.450
What the?!

00:05:23.950 --> 00:05:25.780
Why, if it isn't Tokura!

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:28.320
<i>The girls from the hallway...</i>

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:31.410
So we're in the same class, huh?

00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.870
I know it's gonna be a great year!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:35.710
Yeah. And it's kind of a relief

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:38.750
knowing someone on the first day, right?

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:44.630
Totally! I was so nervous
that it made me hyper!

00:05:44.630 --> 00:05:46.630
I know where you're coming from.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.090
What's this?

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:50.720
You've got something growing on your hip.

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.100
Come on, Kamu, don't hide.

00:05:55.480 --> 00:05:56.900
Introduce yourself.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.770
I'm Kamuri Sengoku.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.650
Nice to meet you.

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:05.320
You're the cutest little thing!

00:06:05.320 --> 00:06:06.820
HMPH

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:11.580
You know, she hadn't grown at all
since elementary school.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:16.330
I'm a late bloomer,
so I grow slower than the average person.

00:06:16.710 --> 00:06:19.330
Huh? I thought you said
you were a growing child.

00:06:19.710 --> 00:06:22.300
You'll be sorry 60 years from now.

00:06:23.300 --> 00:06:24.630
A long-term plan!

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:28.130
If you're 75 years old
and still worried about your height,

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:30.100
you'll be a really petty person.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:35.600
But that would mean you'd still be
friends 60 years from now.

00:06:35.600 --> 00:06:37.810
Friendship that deep moves me.

00:06:39.230 --> 00:06:41.820
I feel like you're forcing it
into a warm, fuzzy feeling.

00:06:42.150 --> 00:06:45.570
I'm moved by my own power to turn
a comeback line into a heartwarming story.

00:06:45.990 --> 00:06:48.570
Come to think of it,
this is really our first time together.

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:52.120
Exactly! Back in middle school,
we were only together

00:06:52.120 --> 00:06:55.290
for the joint classes, P.E. and home ec.

00:06:52.660 --> 00:06:55.290
Those girls are in my class too.

00:06:55.910 --> 00:06:59.500
Wow. They're already so close to each other.

00:07:00.130 --> 00:07:04.380
<i>When I can't even return a simple greeting.</i>

00:07:04.380 --> 00:07:06.630
Hey, get in the room.

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:08.090
Homeroom's about to begin.

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:13.350
First of all,
congratulations on getting into this school.

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:14.760
CONGRATULATIONS ON YOUR FIRST DAY

00:07:13.350 --> 00:07:16.350
I'm your homeroom teacher, Enami.

00:07:16.680 --> 00:07:17.770
Nice to meet you.

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:20.270
Nice to meet you!

00:07:21.650 --> 00:07:24.150
So I'll guess we'll do
self introductions in alphabetical order.

00:07:24.980 --> 00:07:27.610
<i>I had a feeling we would
have to introduce ourselves.</i>

00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:29.400
Ichinose.

00:07:30.360 --> 00:07:31.160
Y-Yes!

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.870
<i>I'm always called first for attendance</i>

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:35.580
<i>and I always have to sit in the front.</i>

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.080
<i>That's the fate of someone
with the family name "Ichinose."</i>

00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:40.120
<i>I hate this...</i>

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:44.130
I'm Hana Ichinose.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.760
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:47.260 --> 00:07:49.970
Low energy from
the very first day of school, huh?

00:07:52.430 --> 00:07:54.760
Ichinose, it looks like today's your birthday.

00:08:04.940 --> 00:08:06.400
Happy birthday!

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:08.900
You're the first birthday of the school year!

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:10.530
Happy birthday!

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:12.610
Happy birthday.

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.450
Th-Thank you!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:20.830
All right. Next, Imai.

00:08:21.460 --> 00:08:26.540
Right. I'm Chihiro Imai.
Um, I was in drama club in middle school.

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:24.330
<i>That was embarrassing.</i>

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.540
<i>I never thought people would wish me</i>

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:28.170
My hobbies are...

00:08:26.540 --> 00:08:29.010
<i>happy birthday on the first day of school.</i>

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:31.300
I'm Kamuri Sengoku.

00:08:31.300 --> 00:08:37.510
I like sleeping and eating
and my special skill is eating a lot.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:39.600
Nice to meet you.

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:42.560
Um, I'm Eiko Tokura.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:44.150
My special skill...

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:48.320
If I have to say something,
I guess I'm good with my hands.

00:08:49.610 --> 00:08:51.610
I don't know about making tons of friends,

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:55.620
but I would like to get along with all of you.

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:56.620
Nice to meet you!

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.370
I'm Tamate Momochi!

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:02.410
Please just call me Tama!

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:05.380
Tama Momochi! I'm Tama Momochi!

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:11.420
Everyone in first-year, class 2,
please think well of Tama Momochi!

00:09:12.050 --> 00:09:13.590
Is she campaigning?

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.640
Well, that's all for today.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.730
Birthday girl!

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:26.730
M-Ms. Momochi?

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.150
You can just call me Tama.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:30.440
Um, here.

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:32.940
It's your birthday present.

00:09:34.450 --> 00:09:37.950
ROAD SAFETY

00:09:34.990 --> 00:09:35.950
A good luck charm?

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:37.950
A birthday present?

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.790
Then here's one from me.

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:43.460
From me too. Here.

00:09:47.170 --> 00:09:49.670
They were giving them out this morning
in front of the station.

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:52.210
You kind of just spoiled it.

00:09:52.960 --> 00:09:56.720
Sorry that's all you get,
but I didn't know it was your birthday!

00:09:57.800 --> 00:10:01.140
None of us did, of course. We only just met.

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:02.850
Oh, that's right!

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:04.850
What? Did you just realize that?

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:08.810
I'll have something better lined up
for your birthday next year.

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:12.320
Yes, next time I'll give you a real present.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:17.530
All right! From today,
I'll start researching what you really want!

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:20.240
That raises the bar.

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.080
I think a whole cake would be good.

00:10:22.370 --> 00:10:24.410
That's only because
you want to eat it, right, Kamu?

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.960
What else would be good?

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.710
<i>I just met them and they're already
talking about next year...</i>

00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.000
A whole cake.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:29.710
What about something spicy. Spicy is good!

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:30.790
No, a whole cake...

00:10:31.340 --> 00:10:34.340
You keep suggesting food.

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:36.050
I know, right?

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:37.430
E-Excuse me!

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:41.430
ROAD SAFETY

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:41.430
Thank you! I'll treasure these!

00:10:44.470 --> 00:10:47.440
You look like someone who really
doesn't want to get in an accident!

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:48.850
H-Huh?

00:10:48.850 --> 00:10:51.310
Now you can feel safe
going to and from school.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:52.650
Thank goodness.

00:10:56.150 --> 00:10:57.280
What's wrong?

00:10:57.530 --> 00:11:00.320
We gave her the road safety good luck charms,

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.370
so now we'll all get into an accident.

00:11:03.740 --> 00:11:06.790
Those charms were protecting us.

00:11:08.250 --> 00:11:10.460
Then we should just go home with her.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.090
That's a great idea!

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:15.050
Let's walk to the station together.

00:11:17.470 --> 00:11:19.050
Maybe you already had plans?

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:23.430
Um, I walk to school...

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.180
I'm envious!

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:26.770
So you're within walking distance!

00:11:26.770 --> 00:11:28.520
You get to sleep as late as you like.

00:11:28.770 --> 00:11:31.940
<i>If I tag along with them now,
they might think I'm strange.</i>

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.100
She probably takes a shower in the morning.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.610
And she can have a leisurely breakfast.

00:11:32.270 --> 00:11:33.820
<i>But... but...</i>

00:11:32.610 --> 00:11:33.820
What's that?!

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:37.440
<i>They're being friendly to me
and I don't want to lose my chance.</i>

00:11:41.570 --> 00:11:46.330
If you walk to school, then you may not have
seen the cherry blossoms by the station.

00:11:46.330 --> 00:11:48.540
They're amazing!

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:50.540
It's like a huge cherry blossom tunnel!

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:51.670
It's really beautiful.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:54.880
I mean, it's a little out of your way,

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:57.300
but how about going with us to the station?

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:01.010
S-Sure.

00:12:07.770 --> 00:12:10.520
Between the entrance ceremony
and your birthday,

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:13.610
it's like you're on a celebratory streak,
Ms. Hana!

00:12:14.360 --> 00:12:19.820
Th-There's no need for the "Ms.",
um... Ms. Momochi.

00:12:19.820 --> 00:12:23.620
Then please call me Tama!

00:12:23.910 --> 00:12:25.160
Tama...

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:28.750
Did your parents name you "Hana"
because you were born in the spring?

00:12:28.750 --> 00:12:29.620
Y-Yeah.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:32.120
That's a cute name!

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:33.630
Oh, but so is Tamate.

00:12:33.630 --> 00:12:36.670
Please just call me Tama!

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:39.460
You're pretty insistent.
You don't want to be called Tamate?

00:12:40.220 --> 00:12:42.010
Just "Tama" has a friendlier ring...

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:43.260
Tamate.

00:12:43.470 --> 00:12:44.430
Tama!

00:12:44.930 --> 00:12:45.890
Tama...

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:48.260
...te.

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:49.520
Ugh!

00:12:50.930 --> 00:12:52.730
You don't like your own name?

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:57.110
Oh, a direct question was really effective.

00:12:57.110 --> 00:12:59.980
No, no, it's not that I don't like it...

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:05.700
Okay, the name Tamate comes from
"tamatebako," a treasure chest.

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:08.790
I thought that might be the case.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:11.960
But Tamate is a pretty name.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.210
No, no, no, no, no!

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:16.460
Let me tell you about "tamatebako."

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:17.290
TAMATEBAKO

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.420
You don't split the word
between "tamate" and "bako,"

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:19.420
TAMATE BAKO

00:13:19.550 --> 00:13:20.170
TAMATEBAKO

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:21.800
but between "tama" and "tebako,"
like "treasure" and "chest."

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:21.010
TAMA TEBAKO

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:22.880
Do you see?!

00:13:23.170 --> 00:13:24.800
My dumb parents!

00:13:24.800 --> 00:13:27.430
They should've thought about it
a little more before naming me!

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:31.270
I was thinking you didn't like it
because of the "treasure chest" origin.

00:13:31.270 --> 00:13:33.770
Like when you open the treasure chest
and become an old woman.

00:13:34.810 --> 00:13:37.400
That's another reason not to like it...

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:40.570
Sorry about that.

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:43.780
But I really do think Tamate is a cute name.

00:13:45.320 --> 00:13:47.320
Thank you.

00:13:48.870 --> 00:13:49.870
I get it.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:51.410
Get what?

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:55.750
Deriving the name "Tamate"
from "tamatebako"

00:13:56.040 --> 00:13:58.290
would be like having meatballs

00:13:58.670 --> 00:14:00.800
and naming someone "Meatba" after them.

00:13:58.920 --> 00:13:59.380
MEAT

00:13:59.380 --> 00:14:00.800
MEATBA

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:02.550
Meatba...

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:04.380
Meatba!

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:05.340
Sheesh!

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.510
I guess I wouldn't like that.

00:14:08.430 --> 00:14:10.680
It's not that funny, Eiko!

00:14:13.430 --> 00:14:16.900
Sorry. Kamu just cracked me up
with that incredible example.

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:21.610
Now that I think of it,
Kamu is also an unusual name.

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:24.610
Yes, it's written as "Kanmuri,"
but pronounced "Kamuri."

00:14:25.070 --> 00:14:27.450
Kanmuri?! "Tiara"?

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:30.950
There must be
an incredible origin story behind that.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:35.460
D-Don't tell me you have the precious blood
of a royal family flowing through your veins!

00:14:35.460 --> 00:14:36.960
Peasants!

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:41.800
Royal family? Actually,
I don't know the origin of your name,

00:14:41.800 --> 00:14:42.960
but I am curious.

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:46.220
I think it's taken from "kanmuriwashi,"
or "crested serpent eagle."

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:47.300
That sounds strong!

00:14:47.630 --> 00:14:50.470
Do crested serpent eagles have a crest?

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:55.140
The crest is the feathers
that grow from their head.

00:14:56.230 --> 00:14:57.440
Like this.

00:14:58.350 --> 00:14:59.400
A ribbon?!

00:14:59.650 --> 00:15:04.150
An eagle, huh?
Compared to that, we're little birds.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:05.990
Little birdie...

00:15:06.150 --> 00:15:07.570
Little birdie...

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.490
That's an eagle's prey!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:17.460
Although I imagine you
more as a predator, Eiko.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:19.040
Really?

00:15:19.870 --> 00:15:21.000
Shall I prey on you?

00:15:22.210 --> 00:15:23.960
There, see?! There it is!

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:28.970
In middle school, everyone knew who Eiko was,
and that name echoed throughout the school.

00:15:29.300 --> 00:15:31.590
She was the most popular girl
in the whole school.

00:15:31.590 --> 00:15:33.350
That's not true.

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.140
Eiko's been making a big impression
since elementary school.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:38.810
Sounds like you've got valuable info!

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:40.850
I'm not going to let that slip on by.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:42.900
Don't you jump on this bandwagon, Kamu!

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.400
They're both exaggerating.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:46.230
O-Okay.

00:15:46.230 --> 00:15:48.070
There, Hana understands.

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:50.910
That's your charm working on her, Eiko.

00:15:49.200 --> 00:15:51.870
<i>I may actually be having a good time...</i>

00:15:50.910 --> 00:15:52.870
Charm... meatballs...

00:16:02.790 --> 00:16:04.380
Wow!

00:16:05.880 --> 00:16:09.380
If we were in a dating sim game,
this would definitely be used for an event.

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:12.970
I'm hungry. I want to eat meatba.

00:16:13.640 --> 00:16:16.560
Kamu, you can say the whole word,
"meatballs," right?

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:20.520
Hey, is there a good café
or something around here?

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:23.810
I mean, next time we can all have tea together.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:26.520
Please tell us!

00:16:27.480 --> 00:16:29.740
A sweets café or bakery...

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.030
And while we're at it,
recommend a supermarket

00:16:32.030 --> 00:16:33.780
that has cheap fish and vegetables!

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:35.780
I-I'm sorry!

00:16:35.780 --> 00:16:40.370
J-Just last year... I mean, this year...

00:16:40.370 --> 00:16:45.590
I just moved here this year,
so there's nothing I can tell you...

00:16:46.590 --> 00:16:47.800
Nothing...

00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:52.590
So that's why you didn't know
about the row of cherry blossom trees.

00:16:52.590 --> 00:16:53.760
Was your father transferred here?

00:16:54.260 --> 00:16:56.680
N-No. I'm by myself...

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.470
You live alone?

00:16:59.270 --> 00:17:00.640
How mature of you!

00:17:00.640 --> 00:17:01.890
That's adulty!

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.690
My cousin is the landlady of the apartment,

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:08.230
so even though I say I'm living alone,
it's like I have a roommate.

00:17:09.440 --> 00:17:11.030
You have a roommate?!

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:12.990
I want to visit you there sometime!

00:17:14.280 --> 00:17:17.240
Great! You're welcome to come over anytime!

00:17:17.620 --> 00:17:20.080
Are you sure? We'll make it into our hang-out.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:22.830
Then can I leave some sweets there?

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:27.000
O-Of course.
You can leave whatever you like there.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:37.760
You're happy you went out of your way, right?

00:17:48.020 --> 00:17:49.610
See you tomorrow!

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:50.980
See you!

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:52.780
S-See you tomorrow!

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:53.610
Bye-bye.

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:06.290
<i>This is the first time friends from school
have given me a present.</i>

00:18:08.380 --> 00:18:09.670
<i>Friends...</i>

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:13.010
Hana! Dinner's ready.

00:18:13.210 --> 00:18:14.380
Okay!

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:18.470
It's a feast!

00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:22.350
After all, it's a double celebration,
the first day of high school and your birthday!

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.600
Thank you, Shion!

00:18:25.890 --> 00:18:27.100
Come on, let's eat.

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:30.900
Thank you for the food!

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:37.160
Hana...

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:40.370
I apologize if I'm wrong,

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:44.450
but have you made friends?

00:18:48.330 --> 00:18:49.710
H-How did you know?

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:53.000
I could just tell by the way
you're enjoying dinner.

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:57.220
I haven't seen you look like that
since you came here.

00:18:58.010 --> 00:19:01.100
I-Is it really written all over my face?

00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.310
In capital letters!

00:19:06.020 --> 00:19:09.310
By friends, I mean... It's kind of complicated.

00:19:09.480 --> 00:19:11.730
I went to see the cherry blossoms
by the station with them.

00:19:12.770 --> 00:19:13.480
That sounds nice.

00:19:14.030 --> 00:19:19.490
But all we did was talk and look
at the cherry blossoms. I mean...

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:23.330
I don't know if it's okay
to call them my friends just from that.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:26.250
Of course it's okay!

00:19:26.660 --> 00:19:28.580
R-Really?

00:19:30.250 --> 00:19:32.880
This makes me really happy too.

00:19:33.170 --> 00:19:36.050
Maybe I'll check out the cherry blossoms
by the station too...

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:37.300
In my old high school uniform!

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:40.890
I-I think you should wear
your normal clothes for that, Shion!

00:19:41.260 --> 00:19:46.270
HANA

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.020
Happy birthday, Hana!

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:51.310
Thank you, Shion!

00:19:51.650 --> 00:19:52.060
Here.

00:19:52.900 --> 00:19:54.230
Your birthday present.

00:19:56.990 --> 00:19:58.110
C-Can I open it?

00:19:58.110 --> 00:19:59.070
Of course!

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:03.200
An umbrella! Thank you, Shion!

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:06.080
Isn't it cute how it looks just like a leek?

00:20:06.790 --> 00:20:08.330
L-Leek?

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:10.460
Here.

00:20:10.460 --> 00:20:13.460
ROAD SAFETY

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:14.000
They were handing them out at the station.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.210
This way you'll be safe
going to and from school.

00:20:16.550 --> 00:20:20.010
W-Wow, I sure will!

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:26.220
<i>You made friends already? That's great!</i>

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:30.230
Yeah. I was really nervous,
but it may turn out fine.

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:31.390
Maybe...

00:20:31.640 --> 00:20:35.440
<i>Yes, you'll be fine! You worry too much, Hana.</i>

00:20:36.820 --> 00:20:38.110
It's getting late.

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.360
It's still cold, so be sure
to keep yourself warm when you go to bed.

00:20:41.650 --> 00:20:44.370
I will. Tell Dad I said hi.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:45.910
Goodnight.

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:47.410
<i>Goodnight.</i>

00:20:50.120 --> 00:20:53.080
Father, Hana says she made friends.

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:55.460
Really? She made friends, huh?

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.420
Good for you, Hana.

00:21:06.180 --> 00:21:07.180
See you later!

00:21:08.140 --> 00:21:09.350
See you later.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:16.820
Well, well, yesterday's birthday girl!
Good morning!

00:21:16.820 --> 00:21:19.730
Yesterday's birthday girl. Good morning.

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:23.070
Yesterday's birthday girl. Good morning.

00:21:23.570 --> 00:21:28.370
<i>M-Maybe they haven't remembered my name?</i>

00:21:28.540 --> 00:21:29.830
I'm hungry.

00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.710
Isn't it early?

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:33.750
We've got a ways to go before lunch.

00:21:32.790 --> 00:21:33.750
E-Excuse me...

00:21:34.670 --> 00:21:37.420
Tama! Eiko! Kamuri!

00:21:37.420 --> 00:21:39.420
I-I'm Hana Ichinose!

00:21:39.420 --> 00:21:42.720
Again, it's nice to meet you!

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:16.310
Oh, that's right! Hana!

00:23:16.730 --> 00:23:18.310
It was the impact of your birthday...

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:20.190
No, we knew it.

00:23:23.190 --> 00:23:24.190
<i>Hana Ichinose.</i>

00:23:24.860 --> 00:23:25.690
<i>Seventeen years old.</i>

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:30.700
<i>I studied a year to get into this school,
so I'm off to a slow start...</i>

00:23:31.450 --> 00:23:35.080
<i>...but my high school life has begun.</i>
